    <p>This is the most compact and affordable RF-mount mirrorless body manufactured by Canon today. It serves as a practical entry point into modern photography and video because it utilizes the exact same RF lens mount found on high-end cinema and pro camera bodies like the Canon EOS R50, R10, and R7. Consequently, any high-quality lenses you purchase now will seamlessly transfer when you eventually upgrade your camera body.</p>
    <p><strong>Reality check for colorists:</strong> 4K video recording is limited strictly to 24fps, and it incurs a heavy 1.6x sensor crop — meaning your standard 18mm wide kit lens turns into a much tighter ~46mm full-frame equivalent field of view. Furthermore, Canon's legendary Dual Pixel Autofocus disables entirely in 4K mode, reverting to significantly slower contrast-detection autofocus. Most importantly, <b>Canon Log (C-Log) is not available on this body</b>, meaning you will need to rely on standard or neutral picture profiles during your DaVinci Resolve grading sessions.</p>
